From 5b4fd127ffddb511b10c51ca75f46e37e6b8c995 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:57:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 72/92] moe-stream, deepseek4, ggml-cuda : runahead's pass
 stands in for the real attention of layer L+1 when every pair of layer L was
 resident at the first half (SiegeLadder G32, opt-in: LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G32=1;
 0 - counted only, the default; 2 - copies built, never skipped)

Then the pass's MoE of L is the exact one bit for bit (multipliers 1, G30's shared rows, the same sum order), so its
attention of L+1 - the stream, the carried mix, the index top-k and every cache row - is the real one. The real block
of L+1 ends in copies of its results into the pass's tensors; the first half of L takes its nodes out of the compute
(GGML_TENSOR_FLAG_COMPUTE, bound per compute by process_ubatch, every flag given back after it) and the pass's values
stand. The CUDA graph key of a split carries the pattern of left-out nodes (needed with G23: a reused split skips the
property check). Not for the candidate source layer or a layer whose input is exported. LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G32_CHECK=1:
no node outside a block reads into it but its copies. Draft: an agent (SiegeLadder docs/v41/g32-design.md).
Checks (oracle o43): G32=1 - text = trace with 11 450 blocks left out (53.8% of 21 280); G32=2 - text = trace; the range
check - 0 reads from outside in 570 blocks. Speed: short context +0.2% (the card draws ~10% less; exact runahead waits
on expert copies), 30K answers +2.3% (ABBA, within the run-to-run spread).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
