+    // SiegeLadder G32 (LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_G32; 0 - off, the default: only counted; 1 - on; 2 - built but never left out,
+    //   for A/B of its copies): when every pair of layer L was resident at the end of runahead's first half, the pass's
+    //   MoE of L is the exact one bit for bit (weight multipliers 1, the same rows - G30 reuses them - the same sum
+    //   order), so its attention of L+1 - the stream after it, the carried mix, the top-k and every cache row it writes -
